    Whack-a-mole round 2 after the ShowcasePage cover dropped the top
    offender: the CRAP gate's next two reds were both #955 network-mode UI
    paths with zero/partial widget coverage.

    - _ChannelRailState._createChannel (CC 8, 0% -> CRAP 72): five widget
      tests over the scripted-HTTP fakes walk every arm — owner happy path
      (POST body, local keypair in the wallet, rail reflection, auto-open
      history page), dialog cancel, empty-name validation, FaNetworkException
      snackbar, generic-error snackbar. _rig now exposes the manager's
      FakeHttpClient alongside the session's.
    - runCreateNetworkFlow (CC 8, 20% -> CRAP 40.8): five widget tests walk
      cancel, dialog validation errors (slug + password length), the no-JWT
      sign-in guard, the create -> join -> live session -> enterNetwork happy
